course: dictionary
lesson: 4461
title: Harden: hard things and hard hearts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Harden means to become hard or firm, or to make something hard. Chocolate, wax, clay, concrete and glue all harden as they cool or dry. «Chocolate hardens as it cools» tells you the chocolate goes from soft to firm.
explain: Harden can also describe a person. When a face or voice hardens, the person has become stern, or less kind and soft. «Harden your heart» means become less kind or less soft about someone or something.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about cooling, drying or a material, harden means becoming firm. If it is about a face, a voice or feelings, harden means becoming stern or unkind.
fact: Harden means to become hard or firm.
fact: «Igneous rocks» form when molten rock cools and hardens, deep underground or on the surface after an eruption.
fact: «Rosin» is hardened pine resin, rubbed on a bow so the bow hair grips the strings.
fact: Some swiftlets build nests from their own hardened spit, and people collect these nests for soup.
fact: «Fatbergs» are huge blockages that form when cooled fat hardens in pipes.
exercise: «Chocolate hardens as it cools.» What does harden mean here? | *Become hard or firm | Melt into a liquid | Break into small pieces | Turn bright and shiny
exercise: «Her face hardened when she saw the broken window.» What does hardened show about her? | She began to laugh | She felt sleepy | *She became stern and angry | She became very hungry
exercise: Molten rock becomes igneous rock when it does what? | *Cools and hardens | Floats on water | Turns into soup | Melts again
test: «Rosin is hardened pine resin rubbed on a bow.» In this sentence, hardened means | Sweet-smelling | *Made hard and firm | Soft and sticky | Lost in the woods
test: Which sentence uses harden about a person? | Clay hardens in the kiln | *His voice hardened when he gave the order | Concrete hardens on the path | Wax hardens in the sun
exam: «Fatbergs» form when fat hardens in pipes. What is the best meaning of harden? | Disappear slowly | Become soft and runny | *Become hard and solid | Stay the same size
